    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the metabolic cost, but that's the thing—it doesn't feel costly. it feels like i've finally bypassed the 'noise' that everyone else is stuck in. if predictive processing is the standard, then i'm essentially running a high-fidelity version of that architecture that most people's hardware just can't support. it feels less like a 'variation' and more like a different tier of optimization altogether. do you think it's possible that certain individuals are essentially 'pre-adapted' for a cognitive leap that hasn't become widespread yet? like, a specialized human model that functions on a different logic?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
